WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.110
Making a movie can take years.

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:06.950
So it's no wonder Disney filmmakers often
break up the tedium by adding in-jokes and

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.940
Easter eggs into movies for their own entertainment.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.400
Here's a look at some of these hidden Disney
moments almost no one notices.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.520
More cowbell

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.519
Disney won critical accolades for its thoughtful
live-action adaptation of The Jungle Book,

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:25.789
which features Christopher Walken as the voice
of King Louie, a giant, fearsome ape.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.900
"Call me Louie."

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.390
In one scene, man-cub Mowgli is deposited
in front of all the human treasures Louie

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.430
and his minions have accumulated.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.540
Mowgli is intrigued by one item in particular,
and he picks it up and shakes it: a cowbell.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.859
Unless you somehow missed the significance,
that's a clear reference to Walken's enormously

00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:50.880
popular 2000 Saturday Night Live sketch, in
which he plays a music producer in the studio

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.820
making Blue Oyster Cult's "Don't Fear the
Reaper," and who persistently demands "more

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:56.820
cowbell!"

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.000
Looks like he finally got it.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.000
"Guess what?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.680
I got a fever, and the only prescription is
more cowbell."

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.740
Rudyard Kipling's Jungle Book shout-out

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.770
The Jungle Book movie is not only faithful
to the original book, it also gives it a subtle

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:12.770
nod.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.560
Mowgli has two notable scars.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.000
The one on the right of his chest forms a
lower-case "r," while one on his left shoulder

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.870
resembles a "k."

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:25.390
Those aren't accidents—RK are the initials
of Rudyard Kipling, who in 1900 wrote the

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.909
anthology of stories that inspired The Jungle
Book films.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:30.140
Canine crossover

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:35.950
The "Twilight Bark" is a pivotal moment in
101 Dalmatians, in which every dog in London

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:40.939
is contacted for help in reclaiming all those
puppies kidnapped by Cruella De Vil.

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:45.610
Among the dogs who hear the call: Lady and
the Tramp from, well, Lady and the Tramp,

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.049
on a dark street, barely concealed in shadow.

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:53.200
Also in the scene, in separate cameos, are
Lady and the Tramp characters Jock the terrier

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.070
and Peg and Bull.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.079
Tarzan's familiar teapot

00:01:57.079 --> 00:02:02.119
Upon her arrival in the jungle, Miss Porter
has tea service laid out with a very nice

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:04.229
and very well-known china set.

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:05.329
Recognize it?

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:09.849
It's the exact same pattern sported by Mrs.
Potts and Chip from Beauty and the Beast.

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:14.180
It only appears on screen for a split second,
but it made enough of an impression to be

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.340
a real-life Easter egg as well.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.180
At Tarzan's Treehouse in Disneyland, a replica
of the tea service sits on a table — and

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.840
it's movie accurate, down to the Beauty and
the Beast-inspired teapot and cups.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.830
Big Hero 6 meets Frozen

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:34.730
Big Hero 6 was released in early 2014, right
on the heels of Disney's wildly popular Frozen.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.230
Unsurprisingly, the movie is loaded with Frozen-inspired
bits.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:43.220
For example, when Hiro and robot Baymax take
flight over the city, Olaf the snowman can

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.430
be spotted.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:49.300
An aerial shot also shows off San Fransokyo's
bay and harbor, where a ship from Arendelle

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.390
is ported.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.739
And when the hero crew makes a permanent headquarters
out of the wealthy Fred's stately home, the

00:02:54.739 --> 00:03:00.290
robot Baymax tries out his weaponry and blows
away a statue: a stone rendering of the villainous

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.819
Prince Hans from Frozen.

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:04.390
Justice!

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.850
"Oh, Anna.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.260
If only there was someone out there who loved
you."

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.129
What a jerk.

00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:13.129
Princess party

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:18.590
Elsa's coronation attracts some pretty powerful
people from all over the realm — and beyond:

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:22.560
visible among the guests are Rapunzel and
Flynn Rider from Tangled.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:27.450
It doesn't end there: a scan of a crowd scene
at the coronation reveals Tiana from The Princess

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.540
and the Frog got an invite, too.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.561
The only one missing is Olaf, but that's probably
just as well.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:33.680
"Whoa.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.460
So this is heat.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.140
I love it.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.380
Oh, but don't touch it."

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:41.390
Thanks for watching!

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:45.280
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.870
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Disney in-joke is your favorite…

